    "durationMs": 337201,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation** (Rails 8.0.2 pinned exactly in the Gemfile, API-only, Ruby 3.4.3):\n- `db/migrate/..._create_links.rb` — `links` table: `code` (string, unique index), `url` (text, so long URLs survive unchanged), `clicks` (default 0)\n- `app/models/link.rb` — validates `url` via `URI.parse` (must be absolute http/https with a host — I probed edge cases like `http://`, `//host`, `ftp://`, whitespace to confirm each is rejected), validates `code` against `\\A[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}\\z`, and auto-generates an 8-char alphanumeric code with collision retry\n- `LinksController` — `create` returns 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}` (URL echoed verbatim), 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on invalid url/code; `show` and `index` (ascending creation order, `{items, total}`)\n- `RedirectsController` — `GET /r/{code}` does an atomic `UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1` then `302` with the exact stored URL in `Location`; unknown codes get 404 JSON everywhere\n- `ApplicationController` — maps `RecordNotFound` → 404, `RecordNotUnique` → 409, malformed JSON → 422, all with an `error` field; also tolerates JSON posted without a Content-Type header\n- `config/database.yml` reads `DATABASE_URL` only; `start.sh` (executable, POSIX sh) runs `db:prepare` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` with no dependency installation\n\n**Verification**: an 89-assertion HTTP suite covering every requirement passed 89/89, then I killed and restarted the server via `start.sh` — links, click counts, and further increments all survived, and `zeitwerk:check` is clean. The database is wiped and port 8000 is free, so the grader's `sh start.sh` starts from a clean slate. The README documents startup and all endpoints."
  }
